# `npm run check` byte-compares the committed generated manifests against a
# fresh build, and the generator always writes LF. Windows checkouts default to
# core.autocrlf=true (GitHub's windows-latest runner sets it), which rewrites
# those files to CRLF on checkout and reports drift no rebuild can clear: the
# build writes LF, and the next checkout converts it back.
#
# Pinning the working tree to LF on every platform keeps the byte comparison
# meaningful and keeps canonical skill bytes identical across platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf
